WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:01.840
- What we're seeing in Beijing here

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:04.380
is concern that Chinese authorities

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.840
may not be able to get
COVID cases under control.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:08.750
In the Chinese capital,

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:10.580
things have actually
been relatively normal

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.490
for most of the past two years.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:14.900
But now with the Omicron
variant spreading so quickly

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.250
across China, and threatening the capital,

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.537
the mood has changed.

00:00:18.537 --> 00:00:21.670
(pensive music)

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.240
And I'm now here at a
supermarket in Beijing

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.680
where they've really
been stocking up quickly

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.860
to make sure that shelves are full

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.810
of fruits, vegetables, meats

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.940
and other goods and over the weekend,

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:35.600
we saw a lot of panic buying here

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.610
as people were stockpiling
and hoarding goods.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.500
People in Beijing were looking at Shanghai

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.420
and the lockdown there that has persisted

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.530
for more than a month already

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.080
and worried about their
own supplies of vegetables.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.780
And so people have been basically filling

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.339
their shopping baskets with
as much as they could get.

00:00:51.339 --> 00:00:56.006
(resident speaking in foreign language)

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.010
- If we do get cases spreading in China,

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.750
that is gonna threaten the economy,

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.240
for the global economy too, of course.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.180
China's the world's
second-largest economy.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:22.400
This is a country that is
deeply tied to the West.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.670
It may have to keep its borders closed

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:26.910
for many more months to
come, perhaps even years,

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.270
and that's gonna have an impact both

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:31.720
on expatriates and multinationals
doing business in China,

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.010
as well as trading partners of China.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:36.400
So the question is really how
much China's gonna be able

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.860
to do to prop up its economy this year,

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:41.210
a year in which stability
is gonna be paramount

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:42.710
as Xi Jinping, the leader,

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:45.296
seeks to secure a third term in power.

00:01:45.296 --> 00:01:47.963
(pensive music)

